1
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:15,610
[poignant music playing]

2
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:19,870
Inako.

3
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:21,150
- Aah!
- [Naeko] Give it a sniff.

4
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:22,070
[gasps]

5
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:24,320
[sniffing] Aah!

6
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:27,080
Smells the same as last year!

7
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:32,250
I love it! Like warm tart apples, 
but it's even sweeter this year!

8
00:00:32,330 --> 00:00:33,830
Very impressive.

9
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:36,050
You're my little master brewer, 
aren't you?

10
00:00:36,130 --> 00:00:38,670
Mmm! I wanna be just like you!

11
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:39,960
[Naeko] Is that so?

12
00:00:40,050 --> 00:00:41,930
Well, then, you need to pray to the gods.

13
00:00:42,010 --> 00:00:44,180
[gasps] The gods?

14
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:46,050
[chuckles]

15
00:00:46,140 --> 00:00:48,600
In order for the sake to be truly good, 

16
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:51,350
we must pray to the gods
to dwell within it.

17
00:00:51,430 --> 00:00:55,430
Only then will it be the kind of sake
that can make your heart shine.

18
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:57,900
Faith is essential to brewing.

19
00:00:59,020 --> 00:01:02,320
We work hard, 
put everything we have into the blends, 

20
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:04,690
and then we pray and trust the gods.

21
00:01:05,450 --> 00:01:07,950
That's the secret to making good sake.

22
00:01:08,950 --> 00:01:10,040
Right!

23
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:11,660
- [Naeko coughing]
- [gasps]

24
00:01:12,410 --> 00:01:14,540
Mother, are you okay?

25
00:01:14,620 --> 00:01:16,910
- [Naeko sighs softly] I'm fine.
- [gasps happily]

26
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,210
- [Naeko] Now let's put our hands together.
- [sighs happily]

27
00:01:23,010 --> 00:01:25,850
[Noriko] Are you all right?
It's so dark in here.

28
00:01:25,930 --> 00:01:28,560
[Inako] I was looking for
Mother's sake brewing records.

29
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:30,180
- Do you know where they are?
- Uh… Oh.

30
00:01:30,970 --> 00:01:33,640
Well, let's see if we can find them.

31
00:01:34,350 --> 00:01:36,270
[Inako] They don't look
like they're in here.

32
00:01:39,230 --> 00:01:40,940
Inako, do you…

33
00:01:41,530 --> 00:01:43,370
want to be a master brewer?

34
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:46,320
[Inako] Mmm.

35
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:51,990
I have faith in you.

36
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:53,920
[gasps and chuckles]

37
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:56,540
- What's going on here?
- [gasps]

38
00:01:56,620 --> 00:01:58,830
- I was looking for Mother's notes and--
- [Jinemon growls]

39
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:00,880
These notes won't do you any good!

40
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:01,840
[gasps]

41
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:05,510
[Jinemon] None of this will do you good
once you're married into the Mizoe family.

42
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:06,720
[Noriko] Father!

43
00:02:09,509 --> 00:02:10,759
[sighs]

44
00:02:10,850 --> 00:02:12,180
That girl.

45
00:02:13,970 --> 00:02:14,970
Mm-hm.

46
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:22,400
Naeko, if you were here, 
you'd know what to do.

47
00:02:23,570 --> 00:02:25,610
[theme song in Japanese playing]

48
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:48,900
SPARKS OF TOMORROW

49
00:03:48,990 --> 00:03:52,950
EPISODE 4: THE STEADFAST GIRL

50
00:03:57,490 --> 00:04:01,200
We'll make this century
the Age of Electricity.

51
00:04:02,210 --> 00:04:04,460
[Yosuke] This… is electricity?

52
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:07,300
This was Seiroku's dream?

53
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:11,680
And now… this dream belongs to me!
[cackles]

54
00:04:12,130 --> 00:04:13,300
[Yosuke] I hate him!

55
00:04:13,390 --> 00:04:14,980
That little brat!

56
00:04:15,050 --> 00:04:16,760
[panting angrily]

57
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:22,270
I looked through the whole book.

58
00:04:22,350 --> 00:04:23,980
It was nothing but scribbles.

59
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:26,690
How was he able
to build the Full Moon? [gasps]

60
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:27,900
Oh, that's it!

61
00:04:28,650 --> 00:04:31,490
The catalog he showed me
must have been a decoy.

62
00:04:31,570 --> 00:04:33,780
Which means that little brat

63
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:36,530
has got the real one
stashed away somewhere…

64
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:39,750
Hah! Bring me a change of clothes.
We're leaving at once!

65
00:04:39,830 --> 00:04:41,830
[gentle music playing]

66
00:04:42,750 --> 00:04:44,460
[woman] Two hiyashiame, please.

67
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:45,620
Coming up.

68
00:04:45,710 --> 00:04:47,710
- [man 2] Here you go!
- [man 1] Enjoy!

69
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:51,930
- [Kate] Ah!
- Cold and delicious.

70
00:04:52,010 --> 00:04:54,640
Everyone's talking about
this steam-cooled hiyashiame.

71
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:56,970
Good thing we passed by the food stalls.

72
00:04:57,050 --> 00:04:59,850
[Suzu] And the surugaya yokan is
delicious too.

73
00:04:59,930 --> 00:05:01,180
[whimsical music playing]

74
00:05:01,890 --> 00:05:05,060
[Kihachi] He took the book with him to war
so he could write all this?

75
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:09,270
I guess I'll be spending the rest
of my life trying to create all of these.

76
00:05:10,570 --> 00:05:12,950
If I do, the Age of Electricity will be…

77
00:05:15,490 --> 00:05:16,740
- [shrieks]
- Hey, Kihachi!

78
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:20,120
- [whimpers]
- I thought you might celebrate with us!

79
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:22,620
M-maybe later.

80
00:05:23,370 --> 00:05:28,170
It would be an affront to the food gods
to let such a wonderful drink go to waste.

81
00:05:32,210 --> 00:05:34,340
It's sweet, cold, and delicious.

82
00:05:37,550 --> 00:05:38,630
[Kihachi] It's good.

83
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:39,600
- [crash]
- [both gasp]

84
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:40,600
Hey, Sparky!

85
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:43,270
- Tell me where the real catalog is!
- Mr. Mizoe?

86
00:05:43,350 --> 00:05:45,940
- Why's the white-haired freak here?
- [growls]

87
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:48,390
- Where did you hide it?
- [Kihachi] What?

88
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:50,980
[snarls] Search everywhere!

89
00:05:51,070 --> 00:05:52,280
- Sir.
- [Kihachi yelps] Hey!

90
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:53,780
Do what you must!

91
00:05:53,860 --> 00:05:55,610
- [yelps]
- [gasps] Mr. Mizoe!

92
00:05:55,740 --> 00:05:57,830
- What the… [shrieks]
- [Izo] Mr. Mizoe!

93
00:05:58,620 --> 00:05:59,870
[Yosuke] Release me at once!

94
00:05:59,950 --> 00:06:00,870
[grunts]

95
00:06:00,950 --> 00:06:02,700
[both] You're not welcome here!

96
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:04,620
Do you know who I am?

97
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:05,620
Wait, Mr. Mizoe.

98
00:06:06,250 --> 00:06:10,460
These two appear to be ex-military.
I won't be able to take them on my own.

99
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:11,880
[snarls]

100
00:06:13,170 --> 00:06:15,170
- [Yosuke] Damn you!
- [Kihachi] What's with that guy?

101
00:06:15,260 --> 00:06:17,050
- [boy] Mommy!
- [man 1] Slow down!

102
00:06:17,130 --> 00:06:19,130
[man 2] Oh, no, is he okay?

103
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:21,760
- Oh, my…
- Hey!

104
00:06:21,850 --> 00:06:23,310
Hey, are you all right?

105
00:06:23,390 --> 00:06:24,890
- [gasps] It's him!
- [woman] Huh?

106
00:06:24,970 --> 00:06:25,890
[trembling]

107
00:06:25,980 --> 00:06:27,980
[Inako] He's the young proprietor
at Nishikiya!

108
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:29,900
[Yosuke] It was you, wasn't it?

109
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:31,650
You hired those bodyguards!

110
00:06:31,730 --> 00:06:33,730
I was their commander in the war.

111
00:06:33,820 --> 00:06:35,740
The two mentioned
they were in need of work.

112
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:37,070
I gave them an introduction.

113
00:06:37,150 --> 00:06:40,110
Don't play dumb, Kuga.
Why are you getting in my way?

114
00:06:40,870 --> 00:06:44,210
Yosuke, you saw the Full Moon
with your own eyes.

115
00:06:44,290 --> 00:06:45,210
[gasps]

116
00:06:48,420 --> 00:06:51,380
I think for now, 
you should wait and let things play out.

117
00:06:52,090 --> 00:06:53,010
[growls]

118
00:06:53,090 --> 00:06:54,470
[scoffs]

119
00:06:54,550 --> 00:06:55,800
Forget it!

120
00:06:59,130 --> 00:07:00,340
[cat meows]

121
00:07:02,390 --> 00:07:05,850
[man whimpering] Banto!
The young master's been hurt!

122
00:07:05,930 --> 00:07:07,850
- Wow, it's pretty dark in here.
- [both] Huh?

123
00:07:07,930 --> 00:07:09,970
[Kihachi] Are they going out of business
or something?

124
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:11,900
[Inako] Kihachi! How could you say that?

125
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:15,280
Nishikiya is a traditional
NIshijin weaving shop.

126
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:16,360
[Banto panting]

127
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:18,150
Young master!

128
00:07:19,150 --> 00:07:20,940
Thank you for your help.

129
00:07:21,030 --> 00:07:24,490
I apologize if this ordeal
caused you any trouble.

130
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:28,290
It's fine, but may I ask
what happened, sir?

131
00:07:28,370 --> 00:07:29,580
On the way over here…

132
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:30,870
Mommy.

133
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,840
…that's all he would say.

134
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:35,710
Indeed, it is a delicate matter.

135
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:41,840
The proprietress of this shop has
shut herself in her room as of late.

136
00:07:42,430 --> 00:07:44,100
Did something happen?

137
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:48,430
[Banto] Sadly, yes. While she was away
dealing with business matters, 

138
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:52,400
her husband, 
the store's proprietor, collapsed.

139
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:54,730
- He passed before she could return.
- [somber music playing]

140
00:07:54,810 --> 00:07:57,230
[Kihachi] It's not like
his passing was her fault.

141
00:07:57,320 --> 00:08:00,620
[Banto] Even so, a melancholy has
fallen over her ever since.

142
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:02,160
- [crying]
- Little Bug?

143
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:04,780
It's because she wasn't able
to be with him when he passed.

144
00:08:04,870 --> 00:08:06,660
- [crying] I'm sorry, Mommy…
- Uh…

145
00:08:06,740 --> 00:08:08,530
- I know exactly how she feels!
- Uh…

146
00:08:09,330 --> 00:08:10,580
Uh…

147
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:12,000
[sighs]

148
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:13,500
- [crashing]
- [yelps]

149
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:14,960
Sir, you can't do this!

150
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,750
- [Yosuke] Nishikiya!
- [all coughing]

151
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:21,090
I think it's about time you lay off
your pathetically outdated craftsmen, 

152
00:08:21,170 --> 00:08:23,170
and replace them with our steam looms.

153
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:25,180
That way, 
you can actually repay your debt, 

154
00:08:25,260 --> 00:08:28,350
and I won't have to close down
your pitiful little shop.

155
00:08:28,430 --> 00:08:33,190
To be frank, I do not have time
to deal with such trivial matters!

156
00:08:33,270 --> 00:08:34,150
[Banto] Uh…

157
00:08:34,230 --> 00:08:35,980
- I beg of you, Mr. Mizoe…
- [Yosuke scoffs]

158
00:08:36,059 --> 00:08:38,190
[Yosuke and Kihachi]
What is he doing here?

159
00:08:38,690 --> 00:08:40,440
Where is the real catalog?

160
00:08:41,070 --> 00:08:44,450
You and I both know you're not
talented enough to build the Full Moon

161
00:08:44,530 --> 00:08:45,700
without his schematics!

162
00:08:45,780 --> 00:08:47,450
[Inako] Stop being so rude!

163
00:08:47,530 --> 00:08:49,570
- Huh?
- [Yosuke] Darling girl.

164
00:08:49,660 --> 00:08:53,790
It's time for you to start behaving
like a proper Mizoe wife, don't you think?

165
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:57,960
Gah! Kihachi is the most
talented person I've ever met!

166
00:08:58,460 --> 00:09:00,630
His inventions are incredible!

167
00:09:00,710 --> 00:09:05,050
It's thanks to him I was able to see
my mother in Paradise one last time!

168
00:09:05,130 --> 00:09:06,050
What?

169
00:09:06,680 --> 00:09:07,680
- Truly?
- [yelps]

170
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:10,100
Oh, If you were able to do that
for the proprietress, 

171
00:09:10,180 --> 00:09:13,680
if only she could actually speak
with her beloved husband one more time, 

172
00:09:13,770 --> 00:09:15,360
oh, I'm sure she'd be cured!

173
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:16,820
Yes, please, sir.

174
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:19,900
With her back, we wouldn't need
those steam-powered looms!

175
00:09:19,980 --> 00:09:22,230
- Right, young master?
- Dada!

176
00:09:22,320 --> 00:09:25,530
[man 1] Please, allow her
to see her husband one more time!

177
00:09:25,610 --> 00:09:26,820
[man 2] Yes, we're begging you!

178
00:09:26,910 --> 00:09:28,120
- [man 3] Help her.
- [boy] Mommy!

179
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:29,870
[Kihachi wails]

180
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,880
[Yosuke] He showed her the dead?

181
00:09:34,370 --> 00:09:36,910
It looks like I was right all along.

182
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,750
That kind of advanced electricity…

183
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:40,800
If Sparky can do all that…

184
00:09:41,630 --> 00:09:43,050
Wait! [gasps]

185
00:09:43,130 --> 00:09:44,550
- [crashing]
- [Yosuke gasps]

186
00:09:47,390 --> 00:09:50,940
- [sighs] I want him under surveillance.
- Sir.

187
00:09:53,390 --> 00:09:54,730
[Inako] A bath?

188
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:57,600
Yep. Invention nine.

189
00:09:57,690 --> 00:09:59,070
The Electric Hot Springs.

190
00:09:59,150 --> 00:10:02,240
Electricity stimulates
the healing properties.

191
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:03,650
- Incredible!
- Yeah!

192
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:06,490
I can't help her talk to the dead.

193
00:10:06,570 --> 00:10:08,910
But one bath in this, 
and she'll definitely feel better.

194
00:10:08,990 --> 00:10:09,910
It's like a dream!

195
00:10:09,990 --> 00:10:11,740
- [crackling]
- Kihachi?

196
00:10:11,830 --> 00:10:13,620
- [Kihachi gurgling]
- [gasps]

197
00:10:14,910 --> 00:10:15,830
[Kihachi groaning]

198
00:10:15,910 --> 00:10:17,790
Everything tingles.

199
00:10:17,870 --> 00:10:19,830
I'm sorry, Kihachi.

200
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:21,510
I shouldn't have pulled you into this.

201
00:10:21,590 --> 00:10:24,510
I think it might be three
instead of eight.

202
00:10:24,590 --> 00:10:26,720
- [Kihachi] Here, let me see.
- [Yajiro] Okay.

203
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,930
I think it says…

204
00:10:30,850 --> 00:10:32,520
It's no use. Damn.

205
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:34,850
The ink is all smudged. I can't read it.

206
00:10:34,930 --> 00:10:36,220
Huh?

207
00:10:36,310 --> 00:10:38,520
So we can't do the Electric Hot Spring?

208
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:41,270
Do you really wanna
put an old lady in this thing?

209
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:45,990
But without it, the proprietress is
never going to get any better.

210
00:10:46,070 --> 00:10:48,780
I mean, I guess we have more options…

211
00:10:49,820 --> 00:10:51,990
Hey, why are you
so invested in this, anyway?

212
00:10:52,830 --> 00:10:56,130
Because I know how it feels
to lose someone so important.

213
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:57,280
- Kihachi.
- Huh?

214
00:10:57,370 --> 00:10:58,830
Uh… [groans softly]

215
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:02,880
Uh… are you talking
about your mom right now?

216
00:11:03,380 --> 00:11:04,340
[gasps]

217
00:11:05,210 --> 00:11:06,670
[men chanting]

218
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:08,050
[Inako] My mother…

219
00:11:09,470 --> 00:11:10,470
[chanting continues]

220
00:11:10,550 --> 00:11:14,300
[Inako] When it came to making sake, 
she was very strict.

221
00:11:14,390 --> 00:11:16,310
But at home, she was kind.

222
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:20,100
She always had a hug waiting
for me and my sister.

223
00:11:20,190 --> 00:11:21,020
[gasps]

224
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:24,020
[Inako] The sake my mother made
was always in demand.

225
00:11:24,610 --> 00:11:27,240
That kept my father busy with deliveries.

226
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:28,200
[chanting continues]

227
00:11:28,280 --> 00:11:31,660
[Inako] The brewery was
a much livelier place back then.

228
00:11:32,820 --> 00:11:37,240
But then, my mother got sick
from breathing in all the soot.

229
00:11:37,330 --> 00:11:38,580
And that winter…

230
00:11:41,830 --> 00:11:44,210
I think about her every day.

231
00:11:44,290 --> 00:11:47,000
There is so much
I still wanted to ask her.

232
00:11:47,090 --> 00:11:48,380
About making sake, 

233
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:50,840
or about the best places
to go on a trip together.

234
00:11:50,930 --> 00:11:54,100
[sighs] There's so much
I wish I could say to her.

235
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:56,730
That's why I want
the proprietress to get better.

236
00:11:56,810 --> 00:11:58,270
So that she and her son can talk

237
00:11:58,350 --> 00:12:00,600
and continue
to experience their lives together!

238
00:12:00,690 --> 00:12:01,690
Little Bug…

239
00:12:01,770 --> 00:12:04,520
You were the one who figured out
how to create the Electric Full Moon, 

240
00:12:04,610 --> 00:12:07,570
so I know you can find a way
to let her speak with her husband again!

241
00:12:07,650 --> 00:12:10,570
You can do anything, Kihachi!
I know you can!

242
00:12:10,650 --> 00:12:12,110
[Kihachi] Uh…

243
00:12:13,660 --> 00:12:15,580
THE 20TH CENTURY ELECTRICAL CATALOG

244
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:18,330
Speaking to the dead is impossible.

245
00:12:18,410 --> 00:12:20,450
I've told you that many times now.

246
00:12:20,540 --> 00:12:21,620
[gasps]

247
00:12:21,710 --> 00:12:23,040
- [Kihachi] But you're right.
- Huh?

248
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:25,620
I can't just walk away from this either.

249
00:12:25,710 --> 00:12:27,800
So we have to find a way to help her.

250
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:29,210
You mean it?

251
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:32,180
[Kihachi] Mmm.

252
00:12:33,510 --> 00:12:35,140
[Kihachi] I'll arrange
for the proprietress

253
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:36,930
to speak with her husband one last time.

254
00:12:37,010 --> 00:12:39,390
You said yesterday
that you couldn't do it!

255
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:40,900
- [Kihachi] I can't.
- [wails]

256
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:42,730
- But I can!
- Wait, what? You can?

257
00:12:42,810 --> 00:12:44,480
[Suzu] How do you plan to do it?

258
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:46,190
Huh? You really want to know?

259
00:12:46,270 --> 00:12:47,900
- Yes! Mm-hm.
- [Inako laughs]

260
00:12:47,980 --> 00:12:51,190
The Electrical Catalog shows that you can
convert electricity into vibrations.

261
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:52,950
- Used to talk to someone far away.
- Right!

262
00:12:53,030 --> 00:12:55,200
- The proprietor pretends to be his father…
- We can do it!

263
00:12:57,780 --> 00:12:59,450
[girls whispering and giggling]

264
00:13:00,540 --> 00:13:02,080
Want to get food on the way home?

265
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:03,830
I could go for something grilled.

266
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:06,420
[Inako] Sorry, I have to get to Nishikiya.

267
00:13:07,130 --> 00:13:08,050
- [Kate] Huh?
- [Suzu] Hm.

268
00:13:08,130 --> 00:13:12,800
[woman] Namu Amida Butsu.
Namu Amida Butsu. Namu Amida Butsu.

269
00:13:13,630 --> 00:13:15,420
- Madam, please listen to me.
- Namu Amida Butsu.

270
00:13:15,510 --> 00:13:17,050
Please listen to what I have to say!

271
00:13:17,140 --> 00:13:19,980
Namu Amida Butsu. Namu Amida Butsu.

272
00:13:26,730 --> 00:13:27,860
[groans]

273
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:29,400
Damn it!

274
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:31,200
[groans]

275
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:35,120
How am I supposed to convert
sound vibrations into electricity?

276
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:42,830
How do I use the vibrations
to make it switch…

277
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,380
[wistful music playing]

278
00:13:48,670 --> 00:13:50,880
[Inako] Madam, please listen to me!

279
00:13:52,340 --> 00:13:54,430
[proprietress] You must
stop this behavior.

280
00:13:58,180 --> 00:14:00,020
[soft hissing]

281
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:02,890
Ahh!

282
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:07,770
It's still not transmitting my voice.

283
00:14:08,350 --> 00:14:09,850
[sighs] This won't work.

284
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:16,030
Please, child, 
just leave me to my prayers.

285
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:19,990
My apologies, madam.

286
00:14:25,250 --> 00:14:26,330
[gasps]

287
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:28,500
Uh… Huh?

288
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:29,580
[Kihachi's voice] Huh?

289
00:14:31,380 --> 00:14:32,550
[gasps]

290
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:43,100
[gasps]

291
00:14:44,640 --> 00:14:47,600
Carbon changes the electrical resistance…

292
00:14:48,230 --> 00:14:51,400
Okay. I think I know
how to make this work!

293
00:14:58,610 --> 00:15:00,110
Please come out of your room.

294
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:02,290
Madam. Come out.

295
00:15:02,870 --> 00:15:04,370
I'm begging you.

296
00:15:04,870 --> 00:15:05,910
[sighs]

297
00:15:09,870 --> 00:15:12,080
- [Yajiro] Is everything ready?
- Yeah.

298
00:15:12,170 --> 00:15:13,340
I guess all that's left now

299
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:16,010
is for the little bug
to bring the proprietress here.

300
00:15:16,090 --> 00:15:18,380
[proprietress] You're back again?

301
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:22,510
I wish to be left alone
to grieve my loss in peace.

302
00:15:23,140 --> 00:15:26,020
Madam, everyone is waiting
for you to come out.

303
00:15:27,310 --> 00:15:29,770
Why do they waste their time
worrying about me?

304
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:32,940
For that matter, why do you?

305
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:34,900
Because… well, I just…

306
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:36,770
I don't want you to have any regrets!

307
00:15:36,860 --> 00:15:37,950
[gasps]

308
00:15:38,030 --> 00:15:40,620
I feel regret every day of my life!

309
00:15:41,530 --> 00:15:44,580
I… I lost my own mother three years ago.

310
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:46,080
[gasps]

311
00:15:46,160 --> 00:15:49,580
[Inako] There were still so many things
I wanted to ask her.

312
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:52,300
But I was just a child then.

313
00:15:52,380 --> 00:15:55,220
I wasn't capable
of understanding what had happened.

314
00:15:55,290 --> 00:15:58,590
And by the time
I finally understood, well, 

315
00:15:58,670 --> 00:16:00,090
it was too late.

316
00:16:02,180 --> 00:16:03,770
Please, madam! Come out.

317
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:06,220
Your son misses you.
He wants to talk to you.

318
00:16:06,310 --> 00:16:08,190
Banto and all the others do as well.

319
00:16:08,270 --> 00:16:11,610
I don't want you or your son
to regret leaving anything unsaid, 

320
00:16:11,690 --> 00:16:14,570
so please come out, 
even if for a little while.

321
00:16:15,150 --> 00:16:16,490
Please, madam!

322
00:16:21,530 --> 00:16:25,410
- [gasps]
- Perhaps you're right, young one.

323
00:16:26,160 --> 00:16:27,120
Oh, madam!

324
00:16:28,490 --> 00:16:30,530
I do not wish for any more regrets.

325
00:16:31,250 --> 00:16:32,630
- [Inako] Thank you so much!
- [gasps]

326
00:16:32,710 --> 00:16:36,340
[chuckle] I see that
the tenacity of youth still exists.

327
00:16:36,420 --> 00:16:38,380
Uh… please forgive me!

328
00:16:39,130 --> 00:16:43,220
Silly girl. It's thanks to you
I am able to leave this room.

329
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:46,640
[Inako] I'm so glad, because…
we're going to speak with your husband.

330
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:47,800
[gasps]

331
00:16:48,430 --> 00:16:49,760
What did you say?

332
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:52,940
Madam, there is a machine
we'd like for you to see.

333
00:16:53,020 --> 00:16:55,770
- Are you saying what I think you are?
- Yes!

334
00:16:55,860 --> 00:16:58,110
You'll be able to speak with your husband!

335
00:16:58,190 --> 00:16:59,940
[gasps] Is this real?

336
00:17:00,030 --> 00:17:01,700
Such a machine exists?

337
00:17:01,780 --> 00:17:03,740
- Of course! It does, madam!
- [gasps]

338
00:17:03,820 --> 00:17:04,819
Yes! Yes!

339
00:17:05,530 --> 00:17:06,950
- Let's go right away!
- Um…

340
00:17:07,030 --> 00:17:08,740
- [yelps]
- Are you all right?

341
00:17:08,829 --> 00:17:12,579
I've been locked in my room so long, 
my muscles have fatigued.

342
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:15,250
- Don't worry, I'll help you downstairs.
- [proprietress groaning]

343
00:17:15,329 --> 00:17:17,420
[breathing heavily]

344
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:19,630
- [Inako] Please, madam, go slow!
- Aah! Aah!

345
00:17:19,710 --> 00:17:21,250
- [Inako shrieks] Slow down!
- Aah! Aah!

346
00:17:21,339 --> 00:17:22,720
- [Inako yelps]
- [both groan]

347
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:26,430
- Oh! Ow! My leg! It's cramping!
- [Inako gasping]

348
00:17:26,510 --> 00:17:28,050
- Inako!
- [both gasping]

349
00:17:28,140 --> 00:17:29,560
Almost there…

350
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:30,980
[both panting]

351
00:17:31,930 --> 00:17:33,180
[both groaning]

352
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:37,860
- [panting]
- Please, have a seat, ma'am.

353
00:17:39,360 --> 00:17:40,700
[Inako moans]

354
00:17:43,990 --> 00:17:45,330
[proprietress sighs shakily]

355
00:17:46,030 --> 00:17:47,570
[soft hissing]

356
00:17:48,280 --> 00:17:49,450
- [groans]
- [Kate chuckles]

357
00:17:52,540 --> 00:17:53,710
[gasps]

358
00:17:53,790 --> 00:17:55,580
Place your ear here.

359
00:17:56,120 --> 00:17:58,370
Then, when you're ready, speak into this.

360
00:17:58,460 --> 00:17:59,340
Mmm.

361
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:02,260
[trembles]

362
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:04,180
[low humming]

363
00:18:05,170 --> 00:18:06,340
[male voice] Chiyo?

364
00:18:06,430 --> 00:18:09,060
- [static buzzing]
- [gasps shakily]

365
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:14,390
Is that you?

366
00:18:16,020 --> 00:18:17,190
[gasps]

367
00:18:19,310 --> 00:18:20,270
[gasps and sobs]

368
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:22,860
You left us all so suddenly, I…

369
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:24,280
I didn't…

370
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:28,780
I didn't know what else to do.

371
00:18:28,860 --> 00:18:32,910
We said we'd make the best shop in Kyoto.
So I worked. I worked so hard.

372
00:18:32,990 --> 00:18:34,330
- I know.
- [Chiyo sobs]

373
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:38,960
I can't do this by myself. [sobbing]

374
00:18:39,040 --> 00:18:40,790
I'm so tired.

375
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:44,590
[sniffles] And I don't know
when it happened, 

376
00:18:44,670 --> 00:18:47,130
but the business has gone downhill.

377
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:49,890
[Chiyo crying] I'm sorry.

378
00:18:49,970 --> 00:18:51,970
[machine ticking and squeaking]

379
00:18:52,930 --> 00:18:54,390
[shudders]

380
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:57,690
You… you don't have to push yourself.

381
00:18:57,770 --> 00:18:58,650
[inhales]

382
00:18:58,730 --> 00:19:01,900
The shop isn't the same
when you're not around.

383
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:04,020
Everyone is sad.

384
00:19:04,110 --> 00:19:06,110
[high-pitched ringing]

385
00:19:08,780 --> 00:19:11,030
[muffled sounds echoing]

386
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:13,250
[voices overlapping]

387
00:19:13,330 --> 00:19:15,330
[poignant music playing]

388
00:19:25,090 --> 00:19:27,800
[boy] I'm here. I want to see her.

389
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:32,430
[Kihachi sighs]

390
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:34,560
[Inako gasps]

391
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:36,180
[Chiyo] My love, I…

392
00:19:36,890 --> 00:19:40,310
I… I promise you, I won't give up.

393
00:19:40,390 --> 00:19:44,770
This old shop is filled
with so many precious memories.

394
00:19:46,730 --> 00:19:47,900
Thank you.

395
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:52,700
[sobs] I should thank you, my love.

396
00:19:52,780 --> 00:19:55,450
Oh, sir! [wailing]

397
00:19:57,950 --> 00:19:58,990
[gasps]

398
00:20:00,330 --> 00:20:01,210
[Chiyo] Hmm.

399
00:20:01,290 --> 00:20:03,460
- My goodness.
- [gasps]

400
00:20:04,170 --> 00:20:06,710
- [Chiyo] Look at the state of this place.
- [both chuckle]

401
00:20:07,300 --> 00:20:10,300
[Chiyo] I suppose nothing
gets done without me.

402
00:20:10,380 --> 00:20:11,760
[birdsong]

403
00:20:13,090 --> 00:20:16,140
Mmm. Akira? Akira, come here.

404
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:18,520
- [all gasp]
- Mother!

405
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:20,640
Why are you all just standing there?

406
00:20:20,730 --> 00:20:22,730
- Let's open the store.
- [all] Yes, ma'am!

407
00:20:22,810 --> 00:20:24,230
[all laughing]

408
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:27,610
- Thank you so much, Inako.
- [gasps happily]

409
00:20:28,940 --> 00:20:31,150
[Chiyo] All right, let's get to work!

410
00:20:31,240 --> 00:20:32,950
[gasps] Did you see that?

411
00:20:33,610 --> 00:20:37,610
You did it! It's like a dream, to be able
to talk to someone who's passed away!

412
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:39,370
- What?
- Can I…

413
00:20:39,450 --> 00:20:42,370
- Can I talk to my mother next?
- Uh, no, that's impossible.

414
00:20:42,460 --> 00:20:44,380
Huh? What do you mean, impossible?

415
00:20:44,460 --> 00:20:47,210
- The proprietress was talking to her son.
- Huh?

416
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:51,720
[Kihachi] Electric Telepathy.
You can talk to people from far away!

417
00:20:51,800 --> 00:20:55,260
What? So you didn't really summon
the spirit of her husband?

418
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:56,220
You can't be serious.

419
00:20:56,300 --> 00:20:57,640
[shrieks]

420
00:20:59,060 --> 00:21:01,150
- [Kihachi] Didn't I already explain this?
- [grunting]

421
00:21:01,230 --> 00:21:02,360
Huh?

422
00:21:03,730 --> 00:21:04,690
Still…

423
00:21:04,770 --> 00:21:08,360
you brought the madam
a lot of joy and closure.

424
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:11,280
That was a really nice thing
you did for her.

425
00:21:11,360 --> 00:21:13,360
Thank you, Kihachi!

426
00:21:15,110 --> 00:21:16,320
[Kihachi] It's no big deal.

427
00:21:16,410 --> 00:21:18,700
- What's important is Electric Telepathy.
- [Inako] Oh, okay…

428
00:21:18,780 --> 00:21:20,280
[Kihachi] And carbon! Yeah, the carbon.

429
00:21:20,370 --> 00:21:22,080
[bubbling fiercely]

430
00:21:23,370 --> 00:21:24,750
[Izo] Mr. Mizoe.

431
00:21:25,330 --> 00:21:27,290
I have a surveillance report for you.

432
00:21:28,210 --> 00:21:30,840
The spirit of Nishikiya's
deceased proprietor appeared, 

433
00:21:30,920 --> 00:21:35,090
and they communicated for a few minutes
on a device similar to a phonograph.

434
00:21:38,350 --> 00:21:40,350
[whirring]

435
00:21:43,140 --> 00:21:44,810
[Yosuke] I have no doubt

436
00:21:46,440 --> 00:21:49,940
that little brat is hiding
the real catalog from me.

437
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:52,190
It's happened again.

438
00:21:52,280 --> 00:21:55,990
Your brother has stolen your ideas
and made them into reality.

439
00:21:56,070 --> 00:21:57,320
[bell dings]

440
00:22:02,160 --> 00:22:03,700
[gasps]

441
00:22:03,790 --> 00:22:05,130
[elevator clicks]

442
00:22:05,910 --> 00:22:07,910
[elevator clanking]

443
00:22:09,420 --> 00:22:10,590
[Yosuke] Huh.

444
00:22:11,340 --> 00:22:14,220
We both know you and I are the only ones

445
00:22:14,300 --> 00:22:17,430
who should know
of the catalog's true secrets.

446
00:22:18,340 --> 00:22:19,800
Isn't that right?

447
00:22:23,020 --> 00:22:24,860
["Soarin'" by Ginger Root playing]

448
00:22:27,020 --> 00:22:28,440
Seiroku.

449
00:22:30,860 --> 00:22:32,900
I swear this to you, 

450
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:35,770
when I get my hands on the real catalog, 

451
00:22:35,860 --> 00:22:38,280
our dreams will come true.

452
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:54,800
♪ Looking up and within ♪

453
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:57,050
♪ To try and move forward ♪

454
00:22:57,130 --> 00:23:01,010
♪ Get back what you gave in ♪

455
00:23:01,100 --> 00:23:02,850
♪ To drag yourself in ♪

456
00:23:02,930 --> 00:23:05,560
[lyrics in Japanese]

457
00:23:05,640 --> 00:23:08,430
♪ Oh, I'll be waitin' ♪

458
00:23:09,140 --> 00:23:11,060
[lyrics in Japanese]

459
00:23:19,150 --> 00:23:23,660
♪ Look at how far we've come ♪

460
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:27,370
♪All together ♪

461
00:23:27,450 --> 00:23:31,330
♪ Soarin' ♪

462
00:23:31,420 --> 00:23:33,420
[lyrics in Japanese]

463
00:23:35,800 --> 00:23:37,470
♪ When I'm with you ♪

464
00:23:37,970 --> 00:23:42,890
♪ Somethin' tells me I'm gonna be alone ♪
